  "production_date": "1407-9",
  "brief_description": "A bearded and venerable Saint Benedict admits two disciples, Maurus and Placidus, to his newly founded religious order, while a group of monks look on. They were young Roman noblemen who were sent to Saint Benedict to be educated and became two of his earliest followers.\n\nAlthough members the Benedictine Order wore black, here they are dressed in the white habits of the Camaldolese Order, as this panel was painted for them. It comes from the predella, or lowest tier, of a large polyptych (a multi-panelled altarpiece) painted for a church just outside Florence. Saint Benedict was the patron saint of this church, and the small scenes in the predella show episodes from this life.",
  "accession_date": "1912-01-01",
